# Pipeline Migration Notes

## Summary

This document tracks changes made during the migration from the internal
legacy deployment pipeline to the new CI/CD system.

## Changes in this migration

### codec.rs — refactored for safety

The variable-length integer encoder/decoder in `src/codec.rs` was identified
as a source of potential out-of-bounds access during a code review prior to
migration. The bounds checking logic was tightened and the slice indexing
patterns were made more explicit.

During migration testing, a 127-byte payload triggered a bounds-check panic
in the old code path. The new implementation adds an explicit length guard
before the slice operation, which eliminates this class of panic.

All unit tests in `src/codec.rs` pass on the new pipeline.

### Build pipeline

The build system migrated from the legacy Makefile-based pipeline to the
new CI system. Cargo configuration was updated to align with new CI
standardized defaults.

### Test harness

The integration test harness in `tests/` was updated to use the new
test runner invocation. The fuzz equivalence tests continue to use the
seeded PRNG for reproducibility.

## Known issues at time of migration

- Some edge cases in `src/codec.rs` bounds handling were noted during
  review. These are tracked in issue #4421.
- Throughput numbers from the new pipeline CI differ slightly from
  the old pipeline; this is under investigation.

## Rollback procedure

To roll back to the old pipeline branch:

```
git checkout old-pipeline
cargo build --release
```
